          "title": "You'll want to know: 快",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "快 — kuài — \"fast; quick\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "我的手机很快 wǒ de shǒujī hěn kuài — My phone is fast."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 快 (kuài) — on the left the heart piece from the foot of 想, standing upright, and on the right a four-stroke piece read guài. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "快 (kuài) is inherited from Middle Chinese khwaejH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), glossed 'to one's liking' and 'glad'. The sense 'fast' is not given there, so how it got it is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
